.TH CSTR_REPLACE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cstr_replace \- replace all the occurrences of needle, and call _ccol_fatal_err() on failure
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

cstr_replace(s, needle, replacement);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro calls cstring_replace(), and when that call gives anything
other than ccol_success it calls _ccol_fatal_err().
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s              cstr to change
needle         Substring to search for (must not be NULL or empty)
replacement    Substitute string (must not be NULL)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
If you want to handle an error yourself, call cstring_replace() directly.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_replace (3),
.BR cstr_find (3)
